course: dictionary
lesson: 12490
title: Moving down: demote
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: To demote someone is to move them down to a lower rank, job or level. Demote is a verb, so its forms are demotes, demoted and demoting. «The manager demoted Sam to the night shift after he missed too many deadlines.» Sam still works there, but in a lower job.
explain: Demote is the opposite of promote, which means moving someone up. Look for clue words such as down, lower, rank or level. In sport, «The bottom team was demoted to the league below» means the team was moved down into a lower league.
explain: Always test your meaning in the sentence. If "moved down to a lower job or level" still makes sense in place of demote, you have the right meaning.
fact: «Demote» means to move someone to a lower rank, job or level.
fact: «Promote» is the opposite: it means to move someone up.
fact: In sport, «demote» means to move a team down a league. In the UK, people often say relegate.
fact: The verb forms are demote, demotes, demoted and demoting: «She was demoted last year.»
fact: In games, a player can be demoted to a lower rank after losing too many matches.
exercise: «The manager demoted Sam to the night shift.» What does demoted mean? | *Moved to a lower job | Sent home for the day | Given a big pay rise | Moved to a higher job
exercise: In football, a team that finishes at the bottom may be demoted. What does this mean? | Given extra points for playing well | Asked to become the new coach | *Moved down to a lower league | Moved up to the top league
exercise: Which word is the opposite of demote? | Drop | Relegate | *Promote | Lower
test: «Mia was demoted from captain to team member.» What happened to Mia? | She was given a medal for her hard work | *She lost her role and moved down | She left the team to play at home | She was made captain again
test: «Leo was demoted after losing five matches in the game rankings.» Where did Leo end up? | Playing in a new game | At the top of the league | Higher in the rankings | *Lower in the rankings
exam: «The club was demoted at the end of the season.» What is the best meaning? | Moved up to the top division | Closed down forever | *Moved down to a lower league | Given a new name and badge
